# Level 5: rings of 6 and 7, ten items. No subset of {6, 7} sums to 10:
# as built, this machine CANNOT rest. It must be re-plumbed — cut and
# re-link belts into cycles whose sizes can absorb exactly ten items.
# One good plan: split the 7 into 4 + 3, then fill the 6 and the 4.
# The win requires every cell keeps an out-edge: a cut that just dead-ends
# a belt makes a jam, and a jam is not a fixed point of a whole machine.
name Surgery
blurb Six-belt, seven-belt, ten items. 6 can't hold them; 6+7 won't fill.
blurb As built, this machine has NO resting state — the fix is not placement
blurb but plumbing. Cut belts and re-link them into shapes whose sums work.
blurb Loose ends don't count as rest: every cell must keep its out-edge.

cycle 0 1 2 3 4 5
cycle 10 11 12 13 14 15 16

items 0 1 2 3
items 10 11 12 14 15 16

mv 3
cut 3
link 3
par 10

row six 0 1 2 3 4 5
row seven 10 11 12 13 14 15 16
